def test_issue_555_baselines_matrix_services_boot_failed_e2e():
    """Issue #555: pin the CLI baselines matrix + services
    BOOT FAILED composition end to end (the boot-failure
    twin of #553). The matrix pins (#427-#455) use flows
    with no services block, the services pins (#511-#545)
    use non-matrix flows, #513/#355 pinned non-matrix
    baselines boot failure, #549 pinned this same
    baselines composition on the SUCCESS path and #553
    pinned the verify boot-failure composition, but the
    baselines boot-failure composition of the two was
    not pinned at CLI level: SPEC.md states services
    are booted before baselines run and "If a service
    fails to boot, the run aborts with SERVICE BOOT
    FAILED and previously booted services are stopped";
    execution order step 4 prints "SERVICE BOOT FAILED:
    <Type>: <message>" and exits 3, and only the later
    dispatch step reaches a matrix flow - SERVICE BOOT
    FAILED exit 3 precedes matrix dispatch, and the
    exit-code table maps 3 to SERVICE BOOT FAILED. In
    code, cmd_baselines creates the parent run dir with
    the -baselines suffix and its services-context
    boot-failure branch (cli.py) prints the line and
    returns 3 before _cmd_baselines_run ->
    _cmd_verify_matrix (matrix dispatch) is ever
    reached.
    This test stubs NOTHING in the baselines, matrix or
    services chain: it stages a flow one level below the
    repo root (so the service cwd ".." resolves to the
    repo root, exactly as in flows/) combining the
    demo-services-http-fail service block verbatim - its
    health path 404s forever, so wait_for_http raises
    TimeoutError at the 5s timeout - with a matrix of
    user [ada, bob] and the #547 setup+steps body, drives
    the real build_parser -> cmd_baselines against a
    temp runs root and ledger, and pins the exit code,
    the single printed line, the run dir name carrying
    the -baselines suffix, the already-created run dir
    holding no files (only the empty steps/ scaffold
    that new_run_dir always creates), and no ledger row:
    run-dir entries exactly ["steps"], no
    per-combination run dirs, no matrix REPORT.md, zero
    files, zero ledger rows and the single stdout line
    together prove no matrix dispatch occurred. It also
    pins the service env exports removed, port 8933 free
    before the run, HTTP-dead after the run via bounded
    liveness polling, and no orphaned fixture process."""
    import contextlib
    import io
    import shutil
    import socket
